From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:57:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: accept a compressed manylinux tag set in
 verify_wheel's filename check

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 auditwheel policy floor sits below our build image, a shape upstream's own cross-compiled legs never produce]

auditwheel's riscv64 policy floor is manylinux_2_34, one below the
manylinux_2_39 build image our workflow pins, so `auditwheel repair`
tags the wheel for both and the filename's platform segment becomes a
dot-joined compressed tag set:
`manylinux_2_34_riscv64.manylinux_2_39_riscv64`. WHEEL still lists each
one as its own `Tag:` line, which is what pip reads to decide
installability, but _require_filename_tag compared the whole compressed
string against that list as one token and never matched, failing every
riscv64 build:

  wheel verification failed for
  wheelhouse/xy-0.0.8-py3-none-manylinux_2_34_riscv64.manylinux_2_39_riscv64.whl:
  wheel filename tag
  'py3-none-manylinux_2_34_riscv64.manylinux_2_39_riscv64' is not
  listed in WHEEL tags
  ['py3-none-manylinux_2_34_riscv64', 'py3-none-manylinux_2_39_riscv64']

Upstream's own release legs are all single-tag (zig cross-compiles
pinned to one glibc floor per target, no compressed sets), so this
never surfaces there. Split the filename's platform segment on '.' and
require each resulting tag to be listed, which keeps the single-tag
case working exactly as before.
---
 scripts/verify_wheel.py | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/verify_wheel.py b/scripts/verify_wheel.py
index 609bc45..f6ee611 100644
--- a/scripts/verify_wheel.py
+++ b/scripts/verify_wheel.py
@@ -154,8 +154,17 @@ def _filename_tag(path: Path) -> str:
 
 
 def _require_filename_tag(path: Path, tags: list[str]) -> None:
+    # auditwheel's riscv64 policy floor (manylinux_2_34) sits below the build
+    # image (manylinux_2_39), so `auditwheel repair` tags the wheel for both:
+    # the filename's platform segment is a dot-joined *compressed tag set*
+    # (`manylinux_2_34_riscv64.manylinux_2_39_riscv64`), while WHEEL lists each
+    # one as its own `Tag:` line. Check every compressed segment individually
+    # instead of the whole filename tag as one string, which never matches.
     filename_tag = _filename_tag(path)
-    if filename_tag not in tags:
+    python, abi, platform = filename_tag.split("-", 2)
+    filename_tags = [f"{python}-{abi}-{plat}" for plat in platform.split(".")]
+    missing = [tag for tag in filename_tags if tag not in tags]
+    if missing:
         raise AssertionError(
             f"wheel filename tag {filename_tag!r} is not listed in WHEEL tags {tags}"
         )
